{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779565290,"nonce":"sdxrTa7+EP53vuuvYl/lF5AK1QM=","title":"Make Channel input prototypes derivable instead of manually serialized input_shape","message":"GraphSpec SimpleFeedback templates currently pass Channel input shape through node params as `input_shape`, and `spec_to_graph()` turns that into `input_proto=jnp.zeros(shape)`. This works, but it exposes an implementation detail in serialized graph params.\\n\\nCurrent behavior:\\n- `Channel` constructs `ChannelState(output, queue, noise)` and its `StateIndex` from `input_proto` at construction.\\n- If omitted, it defaults to `jnp.zeros(1)`.\\n- Delayed channels need the prototype because first outputs come from the queue, and JAX scan carry state must have stable shapes.\\n- Legacy `SimpleFeedback` construction derives prototypes from mechanics/example state and controller output size; GraphSpec templates currently have to hard-code feedback/efferent shapes.\\n\\nScope:\\n- Decide whether `input_shape` remains explicit GraphSpec data or is inferred during graph construction.\\n- At minimum, keep `input_shape` documented/validated for `Channel` and preserve it in `graph_to_spec()` / `spec_to_graph()`.\\n- Preferably, add a graph preflight/prototype inference path that can derive `Channel`, `DelayLine`, and `FirstOrderFilter` prototypes from upstream schemas or abstract sample values before `init_state`.\\n- Do not attempt true lazy mutation inside `Channel.__call__`; it conflicts with JAX scan carry shape invariants.\\n\\nAcceptance criteria:\\n- SimpleFeedback graph templates instantiate without relying on an undocumented Channel param.\\n- Delayed feedback/efferent Channels initialize with correct vector shapes.\\n- Channel round-trip through `graph_to_spec()` / `spec_to_graph()` preserves needed prototype information or can deterministically re-infer it.\\n- Tests cover `delay \u003e 0`, graph execution under scan, and SimpleFeedback template execution with flattened CartesianState feedback.\\n\\nRelated: umbrella 07c0ec9.","files":null}]}